The comment is already close to the code-comments bar (it states a constraint, not history), but it's wordier than it needs to be — the collision explanation restates why truncation is a problem, and "instead" implies an unstated alternative.

<rewrite>
// Postgres truncates identifiers at 63 bytes, so index names built from long
// table and column names get a hash suffix once they exceed the limit.
func indexName(table string, cols []string) string {
</rewrite>

Cut the "would collide" clause — it just restates the consequence of truncation, which the reader already infers from "so names past the limit get a hash suffix." Dropped "instead" since it pointed at an unstated alternative.

